  "notes": "Claude Fable 5.1 same-model effort curves, read from the launch page's inline SVG aria-labels (EXACT values, not digitization) — the same evidence class as the GPT-6 Astra launch capture. Rows are attributed to claude-fable-5-1 only: Anthropic says Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1 are the SAME underlying model differing in safeguards, so a Mythos row would not be an independent measurement. SHAPE DIFFERS BY TASK. On HLE-with-tools the top score is xhigh at 65.1, ABOVE high at 64.8 — high is the cheaper TRADEOFF point ($1.05 vs $2.28), not the best or an equal score; max then falls back to 65.0 at $3.20. On CursorBench and Terminal-Bench Science higher effort keeps paying to max. This resembles the task-difficulty interaction in the Astra and GPT-5.6 ARC data, but it is a VENDOR chart about a different model and is NOT an independent replication of those results.",
